Based on the VoiceOver/JAWS feedback, the root of the issue is that the expandable tile’s container `<div>` is not exposed as a proper button widget (it has no `role="button"`, no explicit `aria-expanded`, and no accessible name that announces the “above the fold” content).  Furthermore, the “above the fold” span has no `id`, so there’s nothing for screen readers to announce on initial focus.

Below are three *SEARCH/REPLACE* edits to packages/react/src/components/Tile/Tile.js to:

1. Compute a stable ID for the above-the-fold content.
2. Wire that ID into the “above” span.
3. Expose the outer `<div>` as a proper button with `role="button"`, `aria-expanded`, and `aria-labelledby`.

